# Full PAM stack for lockme: delegates to the distribution's system-auth.
#
# This is an OPT-IN alternative to the default pam.d/lockme. It restores
# the behavior most other screen lockers (waylock, swaylock, etc.) ship
# with: authentication is delegated to /etc/pam.d/system-auth, so any
# auxiliary auth method or session integration configured there also
# applies to lockme. Specifically, this file enables:
#   - systemd-homed (pam_systemd_home)
#   - GNOME Keyring / KWallet auto-unlock
#   - fingerprint readers (pam_fprintd)
#   - smartcards / yubikeys (pam_pkcs11, pam_u2f)
#   - any other module configured in system-auth
#
# The trade-off is that lockme inherits whatever risk surface system-auth
# carries and cannot defend against misconfigurations there.
#
# To install:
#   nimble installPamFull
# or, without nimble:
#   sudo install -m 0644 pam.d/lockme.full /etc/pam.d/lockme

auth include system-auth
